body:
I was more thinking of the case when the settings look like:

``` php
// In a parent class.
[
  'Crud.Crud' => [
    'foo' => 'bar',
    'active'
  ]
]

// In a child class
[
  'Crud.Crud' => [
    'foo' => 'updated value'
    'active'
  ]
]
```

Since the arrays are not equal we cannot skip merging, but merging will result in 'active' being listed twice as it is a numeric key.
